**Add the eight `MergeEffects` members that `FakeMergeEffects` omits.**

`FakeMergeEffects` declares `implements MergeEffects` at `test/ops/merge/runPrs.test.ts:130`, but it defines only `validateRef`, `fetchRef`, `readBaseRef`, `worktreePrepare`, `worktreeRemove`, `mergePr`, `retargetBase`, and `pushRef`. The interface requires eight more methods: `diffPatch`, `commitParents`, `isAncestor`, `readCommitMessage`, `readCommitEncoding`, `readCommitIdentity`, `objectExists`, and `fetchBaseBranch`. The class has no base class. Because `tsconfig.json` includes `test` and sets `strict`, the class fails type-checking, and the `effects` values passed to `runMergePrs` and `makeRunMergePrsOp` do not satisfy the interface. Add the missing members so the fake matches the contract. The stubs below fail loudly if a test calls them.

